            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Connie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I am currently addicted to Starbucks' Orange Mango Banana Vivanno smoothie, but all the stores in my area are out of them so I decided to see if I could find a replacement! I'm so happy I did because this is EVEN BETTER! This is an incredibly delicious, flavorful drink, chock full o' vitamins and nutrients. I will definitely be making this very often! Thank you so much for posting this delicious, healthy, and simple recipe."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Steve Gloria McGriff"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Easy to make. Fantastic taste and texture. Well balanced blend of mango and banana flavors. Using frozen mango chunks adds cool refreshment. I added 1 Tbs agave to balance the Fage Plain 2% yogurt. I doubled the recipe and used a Vitamix on Smoothie setting. I will consider this recipe as a base “stock” for other smoothie recipes with fruit or veggie add-ins.",
            "datePublished": "2017-10-18T19:07:53.710Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "grpta"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious. I used a couple fresh mangos and a large frozen banana. Added pineapple juice instead of orange and a full cup plain yogurt. This makes far more than I need for a serving but I LOVE it frozen. Pour extra into two-ounce paper cups and freeze. Wonderful 'frozen-fruit' treats.",
            "datePublished": "2009-06-16T14:43:09.763Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "slbrumbalow"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Just made it this morning. I couldn't find the Orange-Mango juice blend. So, instead I used Dole's Orange-Peach-Mango juice blend and it tastes FANTASTIC! Also, an added bonus was that it has a natural sweetness. My mornings are going to start off well from now on ^_^.",
            "datePublished": "2015-08-16T09:20:15.663Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LazyCook"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very tasty. Just made this for my son who had his wisdom teeth removed. The only changes I made were that I doubled the mango and used WF Orange Peach Mango juice as that is all I had. Will definitely make again.",
            "datePublished": "2016-06-14T12:35:17.810Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sandra Luckins"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great base recipe. I used frozen banana and mango. I didn't have any juice so I substituted unsweetened almond milk. I used fat &amp; sugerfree vanilla yogurt. I was a bit sweet for me but then I added a handful of spinach and that made it perfect with the added benefit of getting some of the spinach nutrients. I think this would also be good with strawberries",
            "datePublished": "2017-06-19T18:29:08.503Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sibersong"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent recipe! Thanks. I also edited it a bit: added 1/2 a lime instead of orange-mango juice as well as a tad more yogurt...maybe 1/2 to 2/3 cup. Lime really adds nice zest to it.",
            "datePublished": "2010-05-18T16:31:18.900Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "cookinkitty"
            },
            "reviewBody": "omg, so good. Used one fresh banana one fresh mango (fist time i have never bought and used one) waited a day for the mango to be a bit soft. I washed and half peeled the mango. I added a wopping tablespoon of great value vanilla yogurt and, I dunno, a 1/4 cup dole orange peach mango juice. Also about a handful and a half of ice. I will always have these ingredients in my home from now on. Of course I am sipping on my smoothie as I type :D",
            "datePublished": "2013-05-12T06:36:21.530Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LED87"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was so creamy and thick like a milkshake. We had a few fresh mangos laying around to use up. I added almond milk and left out the OJ. I will definatly make this again.",
            "datePublished": "2011-02-01T12:20:09.580Z"
          },
          {
